Treatment Explanation: Constantly watching traumatic videos has convinced your brain's primitive threat center that you are in immediate physical danger, causing the massive dump of adrenaline that makes your heart race and prevents sleep. This is a severe, physical injury to your nervous system caused by secondary trauma. The medication acts as a temporary brake on the adrenaline, allowing you to finally sleep.
Actionable Steps: Take the medication and go straight to bed. Your phone must remain on airplane mode tonight. Tomorrow, you must enact the curated media boundary; bearing witness is only helpful if you are healthy enough to sustain the emotional load, and right now, your body needs to rest.

